<title>UK: UK M4 grows provisional 11.2 pct in year to March.</title>
<headline>UK M4 grows provisional 11.2 pct in year to March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the following data on UK monetary aggregates for March -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY				   MARCH	  FEBRUARY</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (adjusted)	     1.0	     1.4</p>
<p>	 in year to date (adjusted)	    11.2	    11.2</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (unadjusted)	   2.1	     1.6</p>
<p>	 in year to date (unadjusted)	  11.2	    11.3</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>     societies in billions of stg	     4.5	     8.2</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecasts M4 s/a 11.0 pct yr/yr, M4 lending +6.1 billion stg. * Previously published final figures for Feb  </p>
<p>    Three-month annual M4 rate (adj)	  18.0	 n/a</p>
<p>    Six-month annual M4 rate   (adj)	  13.0	n/a</p>
<p>-- LONDON NEWSROOM ++44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
